Subject: Cantor Candidate Seal and Independent Review Requirement Matrix

@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Candidate_Seal_And_Independent_Review.sop
@ [slice] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\slices\CandidateSealAndIndependentReview.sop

& [MatrixIdentity] is formation and blocker accounting
  + [matrix_uuid] is 5382cd6b-c23a-480b-a957-5b5975849d63
  + [status] is formation_complete_implementation_blocked

& [CSR-001] is source, research, and upstream lineage
  + [support_status] is passed_by_SJS
  + [proof_route] is exact source and research hashes plus Phase3A proof and Phase3B formation

& [CSR-002] is strict commission and root binding
  + [support_status] is specified_not_implemented
  + [proof_route] is canonical strict-schema and substitution fixtures

& [CSR-003] is capability separation
  + [support_status] is specified_pending_API_proof
  + [proof_route] is distinct roots, grants, process types, records, and forbidden-method review

& [CSR-004] is process quiescence and stable capture
  + [support_status] is blocking
  + [proof_route] is live-child, descendant, late-writer, double-inventory, consistency-class, residual-uncertainty, platform-snapshot, and drift fixtures

& [CSR-005] is repository and index invariants
  + [support_status] is specified_not_implemented
  + [proof_route] is exact fixed Git plan and base, ref, common-dir, Git-dir, index, and submodule faults

& [CSR-006] is complete direct inventory
  + [support_status] is blocking_design
  + [proof_route] is tracked, untracked, ignored, deletion, empty, mode, byte, and budget fixtures

& [CSR-007] is path and special-file rejection
  + [support_status] is blocking_physical_proof
  + [proof_route] is case, alias, link, junction, mount, reparse, hard-link, ADS, device, pipe, and socket fixtures

& [CSR-008] is three-view change reconciliation
  + [support_status] is specified_not_implemented
  + [proof_route] is base tree, Git observation, and direct physical inventory equality

& [CSR-009] is atomic content-addressed publication
  + [support_status] is blocking_physical_proof
  + [proof_route] is staging, partial, read-back, rename, collision, capacity, permissions, durability, tamper-evidence, and physical-immutability claim fixtures

& [CSR-010] is capture-only signature
  + [support_status] is specified_pending_key_profile
  + [proof_route] is distinct key, exact signature payload, tamper, revocation, and meaning tests

& [CSR-011] is deterministic reconstruction
  + [support_status] is blocking
  + [proof_route] is base plus capsule reconstruction equality and substitution faults

& [CSR-012] is supervisor-authored contained tests
  + [support_status] is blocking_separate_formation
  + [proof_route] is exact direct commands, sandbox, network, credential, prompt, timeout, child, and output fixtures

& [CSR-013] is complete test evidence
  + [support_status] is specified_not_implemented
  + [proof_route] is environment, executable, command, output, exit, duration, resources, artifacts, and record digest

& [CSR-014] is independent review
  + [support_status] is blocking_fixture_work
  + [proof_route] is immutable-only input, identity separation, deterministic gates, optional-model subordination, and evidence citations

& [CSR-015] is uncertainty and non-promotional disposition
  + [support_status] is passed_by_specification
  + [proof_route] is four closed dispositions and explicit unknown findings

& [CSR-016] is quarantine without cleanup or retry
  + [support_status] is passed_by_specification_pending_API_review
  + [proof_route] is lifecycle and absence of reset, clean, delete, overwrite, reuse, or retry methods

& [CSR-017] is Phase3D evidence-only handoff
  + [support_status] is blocking_specification_dependency
  + [proof_route] is separately governed Phase3D formation and digest-link fixtures

& [CSR-018] is global preservation
  + [support_status] is pending_implementation
  + [proof_route] is all prior tests, release, lint, docs, audit, evidence, and rollback
